{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"492423553055931673f361b6fb74533c2b6010547bab018285d416851d581bb9","digest":{"component_or_area":"DC adapter structural testing","key_entities":["test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py","test_no_search_issues_call_relies_on_the_default_page_size","_TRANSPORT_SRC","_search_issues_calls_taking_the_default","adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/_base.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py","search_issues","maxResults"],"problem_keywords":["structural guard","vacuous test","module split","ast scan","pagination","search_issues"],"propositions":["After ticket 465d's module split, search_issues call sites were moved out of transport.py into _base.py and _issues.py, but the structural guard still scans only transport.py, rendering it vacuous.","The guard test asserts no unpaginated search_issues calls exist, but now always passes because the single-file scan target contains zero such calls.","Widening the scan from transport.py to all modules in adapters/jira_datacenter/ would restore the guard's ability to detect unpaginated calls in any DC adapter module.","A non-vacuity assertion is needed to ensure future module relocations do not silently empty the scan population again."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787332097409627001,"uuid":"6098cf17-c14b-49f4-9d9d-e1d88c2a86a1"}